{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/sizewell-b-power-plant-given-lifetime-extension-to-2055","content_id":"74dd68a4-7180-45d7-8ff2-bcca431ddce6","description":"Sizewell B power plant given 20‑year lifetime extension to continue operating until 2055.","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><div class=\"call-to-action\">\n  <ul>\n    <li>Sizewell B nuclear power station to continue operating until 2055, powering millions of homes with clean, homegrown energy and cutting costs for consumers</li>\n    <li>Government agreed terms with EDF to support 20‑year life extension of Sizewell B</li>\n    <li>Extension estimated to support around 900 skilled nuclear jobs on site</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n\n<p>Millions of households and businesses will continue benefitting from homegrown, clean power as the government backs a 20-year lifetime extension of Sizewell B nuclear power station, supporting 900 skilled jobs as part of a new ‘golden age’ of nuclear.</p>\n\n<p>Consumers are set to benefit for decades to come, as the extended operation will reduce the costs of Britain’s energy system compared to building alternative generation, protecting billpayers and strengthening our energy security. </p>\n\n<p>Currently, Sizewell B provides approximately 3% of the UK’s total electricity needs. The extension of the plant will maintain a vital source of energy for Britain, powering 2.5 million homes and protecting billpayers from exposure to volatile fossil fuel markets through secure, reliable, clean power. </p>\n\n<p>Alongside the extension of Sizewell B, the government is continuing to back nuclear projects across the UK, including <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/wylfa-confirmed-as-site-for-uks-first-small-modular-reactor\">Britain’s first small modular reactors</a> in Anglesey, and the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/sizewell-c-gets-green-light-with-final-investment-decision\">construction of Sizewell C</a>, set to produce clean power for the equivalent of 6 million homes and support 17,000 jobs at peak construction.</p>\n\n<p>Energy Secretary Ed Miliband said:</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p class=\"last-child\">Nuclear power is vital for our energy security, and this extension will help produce the clean power our country needs.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer, Rachel Reeves, said:</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>Sizewell B is a vital part of Britain’s energy future, and this agreement secures clean, homegrown power for millions of homes until 2055</p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">It is also a real vote of confidence in the hundreds of skilled workers in Suffolk who will power Britain’s clean energy future, delivering the long-term certainty that businesses and workers need.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>Minister for Science, Innovation, Research and Nuclear Lord Vallance said:</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>This deal protects billpayers and boosts the country’s energy security by continuing to provide clean, secure power for millions of households.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">By backing Sizewell B, we are delivering a golden age of nuclear and maintaining 900 skilled jobs in Suffolk.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>The government and EDF have agreed terms for a 20-year Contract for Difference at £70.50 per megawatt hour in 2025 prices starting from 2035, the original closure date, with support and investment from Centrica.  </p>\n\n<p>Skilled workers in nuclear will be retained through the continued operation of Sizewell B, helping to sustain Britain’s expertise and strengthening homegrown supply chains. The Nuclear Industry Association estimates that nearly 100,000 people are employed in nuclear jobs across the country. </p>\n\n<p>New estimates suggest that had Sizewell B been operating under this agreement during the energy price crisis following Russia’s invasion of Ukraine, consumers would have saved around £2 billion.</p>\n\n<p>Simone Rossi, CEO of EDF UK, said:</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p class=\"last-child\">Global events demonstrate time and again how vital it is for the UK to secure long term, low-carbon, homegrown electricity which protects British households and businesses from market volatility. Extending the life of the plants we already have alongside building new ones is central to EDF’s strategy.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>Chris O’Shea, Chief Executive of Centrica said:</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p class=\"last-child\">I’m delighted that Sizewell B, in which Centrica owns a 20% share, will continue to play a key role in the UK’s energy system for decades to come. Generating around 3% of the UK’s electricity, Sizewell B is critical to delivering the reliable, zero-carbon baseload power that supports Britain’s energy security, protects skilled jobs and underpins a more resilient economy. We welcome the constructive engagement with government in reaching this agreement, providing the certainty needed to support the required investment.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<h2 id=\"notes-to-editor\">Notes to editor</h2>\n\n<p>While we have reached agreement on the Head of Terms, the final deal will be subject to development of the long-form contract and all regulatory approvals. This will be announced in due course.</p>\n\n<p>Centrica, which owns a 20% stake in Sizewell B, has supported the agreement and the investment required to enable the station to operate through to 2055.</p>\n\n<p>New estimates suggest that had Sizewell B been operating under this agreement during the energy price crisis following Russia’s invasion of Ukraine, consumers would have saved around £2 billion – based on 2025 prices.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-08T21:30:00Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["6315817c-ef11-4905-bb4d-b6dca8e9052c"],"images":[{"caption":"","content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a4e7e66559c26eacf438f79/s216_GFX2607-222-Sizewell.jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a4e7e6606e7256c331df878/s300_GFX2607-222-Sizewell.jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a4e7e666dc61525ffaacf7b/s465_GFX2607-222-Sizewell.jpg","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a4e7e6606e7256c331df877/s630_GFX2607-222-Sizewell.jpg","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a4e7e6606e7256c331df876/s712_GFX2607-222-Sizewell.jpg","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a4e7e66f79c9db2eb438f6a/s960_GFX2607-222-Sizewell.jpg"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"press_release","first_published_at":"2026-07-08T22:30:00+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/sizewell-b-power-plant-given-lifetime-extension-to-2055","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/sizewell-b-power-plant-given-lifetime-extension-to-2055","base_path":"/government/news/sizewell-b-power-plant-given-lifetime-extension-to-2055","content_id":"74dd68a4-7180-45d7-8ff2-bcca431ddce6","document_type":"press_release","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-08T21:30:00Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"Sizewell B power plant given lifetime extension to 2055","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/sizewell-b-power-plant-given-lifetime-extension-to-2055","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1380","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","base_path":"/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","content_id":"6315817c-ef11-4905-bb4d-b6dca8e9052c","details":{"acronym":"DESNZ","brand":"department-for-energy-security-net-zero","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/656df1fd1104cf000dfa74a1/s960_whitehall-place-exterior-960x640.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/656df1fd0f12ef07a53e01be/s300_whitehall-place-exterior-960x640.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Department for<br/>Energy Security<br/>&amp; Net Zero"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Department for Energy Security and Net Zero","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","withdrawn":false}],"government":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","base_path":"/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","content_id":"9dbff654-cdeb-4ebe-9a12-cd4cc20a033e","details":{"current":false,"ended_on":"2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00","started_on":"2024-07-05T00:00:00+00:00"},"document_type":"government","links":{},"locale":"en","title":"2024 to 2026 Starmer Labour government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/2024-starmer-labour-government"}],"organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1380","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","base_path":"/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","content_id":"6315817c-ef11-4905-bb4d-b6dca8e9052c","details":{"acronym":"DESNZ","brand":"department-for-energy-security-net-zero","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/656df1fd1104cf000dfa74a1/s960_whitehall-place-exterior-960x640.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/656df1fd0f12ef07a53e01be/s300_whitehall-place-exterior-960x640.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Department for<br/>Energy Security<br/>&amp; Net Zero"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Department for Energy Security and Net Zero","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","withdrawn":false}],"people":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/rachel-reeves","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/rachel-reeves","base_path":"/government/people/rachel-reeves","content_id":"18ff123b-9f73-4e6d-98a2-a693ecefbc37","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-20T17:48:57Z","schema_name":"person","title":"The Rt Hon Rachel Reeves MP","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/rachel-reeves","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/ed-miliband","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/ed-miliband","base_path":"/government/people/ed-miliband","content_id":"0fdeeed1-bdca-46f9-b6f2-1aade6bf10e0","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-20T17:56:00Z","schema_name":"person","title":"The Rt Hon Ed Miliband MP","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/ed-miliband","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/patrick-vallance","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/patrick-vallance","base_path":"/government/people/patrick-vallance","content_id":"5fc1461f-7d9f-4cb9-b14e-4bf63afb9d92","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-22T10:18:39Z","schema_name":"person","title":"Lord Vallance","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/patrick-vallance","withdrawn":false}],"primary_publishing_organisation":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1380","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","base_path":"/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","content_id":"6315817c-ef11-4905-bb4d-b6dca8e9052c","details":{"acronym":"DESNZ","brand":"department-for-energy-security-net-zero","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/656df1fd1104cf000dfa74a1/s960_whitehall-place-exterior-960x640.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/656df1fd0f12ef07a53e01be/s300_whitehall-place-exterior-960x640.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Department for<br/>Energy Security<br/>&amp; Net Zero"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Department for Energy Security and Net Zero","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-energy-security-and-net-zero","withdrawn":false}],"roles":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/chancellor-of-the-exchequer","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/chancellor-of-the-exchequer","base_path":"/government/ministers/chancellor-of-the-exchequer","content_id":"845e5c6b-c0f1-11e4-8223-005056011aef","details":{"body":"<p>The Chancellor of the Exchequer is the government’s chief financial minister and is responsible for growing the UK economy, raising revenue through taxation or borrowing and for controlling public spending. He has overall responsibility for the work of the Treasury. </p>\n\n<p>The Chancellor’s responsibilities cover:  </p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>\n    <p>Economic and fiscal policy (including presenting the annual Budget) </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Oversight of the monetary framework, including setting the inflation remit, and liaison with the Governor of the Bank of England on monetary policy </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>UK growth and productivity, including working across government on innovation, new technologies, skills, labour markets, migration and competition.   </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>UK public financial institutions  </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Capital markets and listings </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Leading on international economic and financial affairs including at the G7 and G20 and acting as the UK Governor of the IMF, EBRD and AIIB.  </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Economic security and resilience policy </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>International defence and security financing</p>\n  </li>\n</ul>\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":8,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-08-14T17:12:00Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Chancellor of the Exchequer","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/chancellor-of-the-exchequer","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/secretary-of-state","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/secretary-of-state","base_path":"/government/ministers/secretary-of-state","content_id":"acde07a8-5971-4b2c-a34c-5ad9eed5ef9d","details":{"body":"<p>The Secretary of State has overall responsibility for the Department for Energy Security and Net Zero.</p>\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":20,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2023-02-28T11:43:03Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Secretary of State for Energy Security and Net Zero","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/secretary-of-state","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/minister-of-state-for-science-research-and-innovation","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/minister-of-state-for-science-research-and-innovation","base_path":"/government/ministers/minister-of-state-for-science-research-and-innovation","content_id":"ec0f0dbc-4403-4e28-ac0d-a3e09ac4fa9e","details":{"body":"<p>The Minister of State for Science, Research and Innovation is responsible for:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Domestic science and research ecosystem, including Public Sector Research Establishments (<abbr title=\"Public Sector Research Establishments\">PSREs</abbr>)</li>\n  <li>International science and research, including space science</li>\n  <li>Horizon Europe </li>\n  <li><abbr title=\"Research and Development\">R&amp;D</abbr></li>\n  <li>Life sciences </li>\n  <li>Quantum, engineering biology and semiconductors</li>\n  <li>\n<a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/advanced-research-and-invention-agency\">Advanced Research and Invention Agency</a> (<abbr title=\"Advanced Research and Invention Agency\">ARIA</abbr>) </li>\n  <li>\n<a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/government-office-for-technology-transfer\">Government Office for Technology Transfer</a> (<abbr title=\"Government Office for Technology Transfer\">GOTT</abbr>) </li>\n  <li>\n<a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://www.ukri.org/\">UK Research and Innovation</a> (<abbr title=\"UK Research and Innovation\">UKRI</abbr>) </li>\n  <li>Tech and innovation across the missions</li>\n  <li>Regulatory Innovation Office</li>\n  <li>Oxford – Cambridge Growth Corridor Champion</li>\n</ul>\n\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":100,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2025-03-04T17:26:10Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Minister of State for Science, Research and Innovation","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/minister-of-state-for-science-research-and-innovation","withdrawn":false}],"taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/environment/low-carbon-technologies","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/environment/low-carbon-technologies","base_path":"/environment/low-carbon-technologies","content_id":"5812ef82-6a5c-43b8-9d76-b3f7d8019945","details":{"internal_name":"Low carbon technologies [P]","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"parent_taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/environment/climate-change-energy-energy-infrastructure","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/environment/climate-change-energy-energy-infrastructure","base_path":"/environment/climate-change-energy-energy-infrastructure","content_id":"899d76d6-4d59-409e-a7a4-2a7e47c9361b","details":{"internal_name":"Energy infrastructure [T]","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"parent_taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/environment","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/environment","base_path":"/environment","content_id":"3cf97f69-84de-41ae-bc7b-7e2cc238fa58","description":"","details":{"internal_name":"Environment","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":true},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"root_taxon":[{"api_path":"/api/content/","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/","base_path":"/","content_id":"f3bbdec2-0e62-4520-a7fd-6ffd5d36e03a","document_type":"homepage","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-02-18T13:00:23Z","schema_name":"homepage","title":"GOV.UK homepage","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2018-09-16T13:39:00Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Environment","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/environment","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2018-09-05T16:13:09Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Energy infrastructure","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/environment/climate-change-energy-energy-infrastructure","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2018-09-05T16:13:09Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Low carbon technologies","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/environment/low-carbon-technologies","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2026-07-08T22:30:00+01:00","publishing_app":"whitehall","publishing_request_id":"22-1783587370.234-10.13.20.31-2959","publishing_scheduled_at":"2026-07-08T22:30:00+01:00","rendering_app":"frontend","scheduled_publishing_delay_seconds":6,"schema_name":"news_article","title":"Sizewell B power plant given lifetime extension to 2055","updated_at":"2026-09-16T12:42:00+01:00","withdrawn_notice":{}}